### What happens next

The IXP model itself is done and published. The remaining steps to complete your end-to-end automation are **product-side** steps I can point you toward:

1. **Deploy the model to an Orchestrator folder** — this makes it available to downstream automations. Do this in-product: [Building & Deploying Models](https://docs.uipath.com/ixp/automation-cloud/latest/user-guide/building-and-deploying-models)

2. **Build the RPA workflow** — a UiPath process that:
   - Watches your email/shared folder for new invoice PDFs
   - Sends each PDF through this IXP model to extract the 20 fields
   - Posts the structured data into SAP (via SAP connector or UI automation)

   For this step I can hand you off to the **UiPath RPA** skill if you'd like help building that automation.

